            <ArticleTitle>[Arteritis as the cause of fatal coronary thrombosis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2324-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Arteritis of the coronary arteries is a rare phenomenon. The cause is not always known. Transient ischaemia and even thrombosis of the arteries may be seen. The case of a 35 year-old man who died following myocardial infarction are presented and discussed. Even younger people with severe chest pain ought to be hospitalized immediately.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
